#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078164 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078577 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d21b4ce3-d80e-5894-92ce-668e64d91649" :knowledge-point/title "Clearing a Rational Expression With a Variable on One Side"}] :question/id #uuid "7adb1612-0903-5a50-b5cd-75ebf1d0dd4a" :question/math-academy-id "e-12854" :question/problem "Solve the equation $13 = \\dfrac{6y+8}{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we clear the rational expression by multiplying both sides by $2\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t13 &= \\dfrac{6y+8}{2} \\\n\t\t2 \\cdot 13 &= 2 \\cdot \\left(\\dfrac{6y+8}{2}\\right)  \\   \n\t\t2 \\cdot 13 &= \\cancel{2} \\cdot \\left(\\dfrac{6y+8}{\\cancel{2}}\\right) \\   \n\t\t26 &= 6y+8\n\t}\n$$\n\nNext, we solve the remaining equation using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t26 &= 6y+8 \\\n\t\t26-8 &= 6y+8-8 \\\n\t\t18 &= 6y \\\n\t\t\\dfrac{18}{6} &= \\dfrac{6y}{6} \\\n\t\t3 &= y\n\t}\n$$\n\nThus, $y=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078165 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078578 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d31a29c9-e053-557b-8f5a-3dd49b340144" :knowledge-point/title "Clearing a Rational Expression With a Variable on Both Sides"}] :question/id #uuid "c176f07d-e4ee-5f8a-8b7c-7b1c62898bd8" :question/math-academy-id "e-12855" :question/problem "Solve the equation $\\dfrac{a+2}{3} =a.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we clear the rational expression by multiplying both sides by $3\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\require{cancel}\n\t\\eqalign{\n\\dfrac{a+2}{3} &=a \\\n3 \\cdot \\left( \\dfrac{a+2}{3} \\right) &= 3 \\cdot a \\\n\\cancel{3} \\cdot \\left( \\dfrac{a+2}{ \\cancel{3} } \\right) &= 3a \\\na+2 &= 3a\n\t}\n$$\n\nNext, we solve the remaining equation using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\require{cancel}\n\t\\eqalign{\na+2 &= 3a \\\na + 2 - a &= 3a - a \\\n2 &= 2a \\\n\\dfrac{2}{2} &= \\dfrac{2a}{2} \\\n1 &= a\n\t}\n$$\n\nThus, $a=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078166 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078579 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9d60309-32e0-535d-b5fa-ef55787336c8" :knowledge-point/title "Clearing a Rational Expression With Binomials on Both Sides"}] :question/id #uuid "31f9d893-26fd-5b2e-9730-57c5e6cc0615" :question/math-academy-id "e-12857" :question/problem "Solve the equation $\\dfrac{2n+6}{3} = 4n+1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we clear the rational expression by multiplying both sides by $3.$ We must make sure that *all* of the terms on the right-hand side are multiplied by $3.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2n+6}{3} & =4n+1 \\\\ 3\\cdot (\\frac{2n+6}{3}) & =3\\cdot (4n+1) \\\\ \\cancel{3}\\cdot (\\frac{2n+6}{\\cancel{3}}) & =3\\cdot 4n+3\\cdot 1 \\\\ 2n+6 & =12n+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we solve the remaining equation using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2n+6 & =12n+3 \\\\ 2n+6-2n & =12n+3-2n \\\\ 6 & =10n+3 \\\\ 6-3 & =10n+3-3 \\\\ 3 & =10n \\\\ \\frac{3}{10} & =\\frac{10n}{10} \\\\ \\frac{3}{10} & =n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $n = \\dfrac{3}{10}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078167 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078580 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f22f7b2-16a9-5742-9bef-c26d774c85de" :knowledge-point/title "Clearing a Rational Expression That Includes a Factored Expression"}] :question/id #uuid "de18238b-ec8a-525d-b886-b869aa736d56" :question/math-academy-id "e-12858" :question/problem "Solve $\\dfrac{5p+10}{6} =2(p-5).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we clear the rational expression by multiplying both sides by $6\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac{5p+10}{6} &=2(p-5)\\\n\t\t6 \\cdot \\left(\\dfrac{5p+10}{6}\\right) &=6\\cdot 2 (p-5) \\   \n\t\t\\cancel{6} \\cdot \\left(\\dfrac{5p+10}{\\cancel{6}}\\right) &=12(p-5) \\   \n\t\t5p+10 &=12p-60\n\t}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve the remaining equation using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t5p+10 &=12p-60 \\\n\t\t5p+10-5p &=12p-60-5p \\\n\t\t10 &=7p-60 \\\n\t\t10+60 &=7p-60+60 \\\n\t\t70 &=7p \\\n\t\t\\dfrac{70}{7} &=\\dfrac{7p}{7} \\\n\t\t10 &= p\n\t}\n$$\n\nThus, $p=10.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487314 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078578 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d31a29c9-e053-557b-8f5a-3dd49b340144" :knowledge-point/title "Clearing a Rational Expression With a Variable on Both Sides"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11d6e9c3-191d-5438-b906-5d1d3cc45e81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "w=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486633} {:answer/id #uuid "5a76661f-dbc7-54d2-a811-7f13e3306e5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "w=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486794} {:answer/id #uuid "c7c72bd5-cce7-5120-98f8-83a5c9c7dd55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "w=\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487036} {:answer/id #uuid "edfd9eaf-6828-5668-b6aa-9b9fd0b739b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "w=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487100} {:answer/id #uuid "faf764a5-4476-5534-af8f-d57d52fd0ca9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "w=-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487133}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11d6e9c3-191d-5438-b906-5d1d3cc45e81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "w=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486633} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d661ec7-ecd8-5468-bb3e-4657cb6057cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487216}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "31ff821e-8692-536f-977f-3df1a10cce49" :question/math-academy-id "q-101638" :question/problem "Solve the equation $\\frac{7w+10}{3}=4w.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we clear the rational expression by multiplying the equation through by $3$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7w+10}{3} & =4w \\\\ 3(\\frac{7w+10}{3}) & =3\\cdot (4w) \\\\ \\cancel{3}\\cdot (\\frac{7w+10}{\\cancel{3}}) & =12w \\\\ 7w+10 & =12w\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve the remaining equation using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7w+10 & =12w \\\\ 7w+10-7w & =12w-7w \\\\ 10 & =5w \\\\ \\frac{10}{5} & =\\frac{5w}{5} \\\\ 2 & =w\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $w=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487373 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078580 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f22f7b2-16a9-5742-9bef-c26d774c85de" :knowledge-point/title "Clearing a Rational Expression That Includes a Factored Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32deff54-cf1b-51d8-98a8-17edf2755d74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=-\\frac{5}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486702} {:answer/id #uuid "34a63bf2-dc91-5faa-acd3-2a97efc245c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486706} {:answer/id #uuid "371b284e-75fc-5ae0-805b-4dfcf7fe1204" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486711} {:answer/id #uuid "bc0f1775-39be-5d30-a765-a264293338f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487006} {:answer/id #uuid "dbf9705c-c47b-5a06-8ca9-7a40b09a14b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487073}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "371b284e-75fc-5ae0-805b-4dfcf7fe1204" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486711} :answer-field/id #uuid "87558509-bc3d-5cff-8d80-67471b464e32" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487215}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ba37a28b-262f-5934-93da-824b60873e74" :question/math-academy-id "q-101642" :question/problem "Solve for $t$ where $3(2t-1)=\\frac{4t-3}{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we clear the rational expression by multiplying the equation through by $2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(2t-1) & =\\frac{4t-3}{2} \\\\ 2\\cdot (3(2t-1)) & =2(\\frac{4t-3}{2}) \\\\ 6(2t-1) & =\\cancel{2}(\\frac{4t-3}{\\cancel{2}}) \\\\ 12t-6 & =4t-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve the remaining equation using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12t-6 & =4t-3 \\\\ 12t-6-4t & =-3+4t-4t \\\\ 8t-6 & =-3 \\\\ 8t-6+6 & =-3+6 \\\\ 8t & =3 \\\\ \\frac{8t}{8} & =\\frac{3}{8} \\\\ t & =\\frac{3}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487340 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078580 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f22f7b2-16a9-5742-9bef-c26d774c85de" :knowledge-point/title "Clearing a Rational Expression That Includes a Factored Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e6d0390-6f5d-5ea3-8acf-4e61f32f370c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=-\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486728} {:answer/id #uuid "4c811b7c-2599-5f3e-996d-248cb7234111" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486759} {:answer/id #uuid "6c6b7565-5ec4-5c69-b184-92b242a17920" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486830} {:answer/id #uuid "7cb66b61-f470-55f4-ae65-74b5aa5faafb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486864} {:answer/id #uuid "c231de60-ae32-5e60-a3aa-6f1d31329ab0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487021}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7cb66b61-f470-55f4-ae65-74b5aa5faafb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486864} :answer-field/id #uuid "3118df3e-2303-5bed-8677-887ac749f191" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487158}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6dc17e55-1c4a-5a93-b3b8-937d5766223d" :question/math-academy-id "q-101643" :question/problem "Solve for $n$ where $\\frac{2n-8}{3}=-6(n+1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we clear the rational expression by multiplying the equation through by $3$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2n-8}{3} & =-6(n+1) \\\\ 3\\cdot (\\frac{2n-8}{3}) & =3\\cdot (-6(n+1)) \\\\ \\cancel{3}\\cdot (\\frac{2n-8}{\\cancel{3}}) & =-18(n+1) \\\\ 2n-8 & =-18n-18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve the remaining equation using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2n-8 & =-18n-18 \\\\ 2n-8+18n & =-18n-18+18n \\\\ 20n-8 & =-18 \\\\ 20n-8+8 & =-18+8 \\\\ 20n & =-10 \\\\ \\frac{20n}{20} & =\\frac{-10}{20} \\\\ n & =-\\frac{10}{20} \\\\ n & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487331 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078579 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9d60309-32e0-535d-b5fa-ef55787336c8" :knowledge-point/title "Clearing a Rational Expression With Binomials on Both Sides"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a9ceb97-7185-5891-985c-632bd2b70a6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486676}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a9ceb97-7185-5891-985c-632bd2b70a6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486676} :answer-field/id #uuid "9161d309-95b3-56aa-8ea9-ac7e501ed385" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487218}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "595c6cf3-442f-5ee5-b303-59b7320fc44a" :question/math-academy-id "q-171596" :question/problem "If $\\frac{3+m}{7}=2m-7,$ then $m=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we clear the rational expression by multiplying the equation through by $7$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3+m}{7} & =2m-7 \\\\ 7(\\frac{3+m}{7}) & =7(2m-7) \\\\ \\cancel{7}(\\frac{3+m}{\\cancel{7}}) & =14m-49 \\\\ 3+m & =14m-49\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve the remaining equation using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3+m & =14m-49 \\\\ 3+m-m & =14m-49-m \\\\ 3 & =13m-49 \\\\ 3+49 & =13m-49+49 \\\\ 52 & =13m \\\\ \\frac{52}{13} & =\\frac{13m}{13} \\\\ 4 & =\\frac{\\cancel{13}m}{\\cancel{13}} \\\\ 4 & =m \\\\ m & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487304 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078577 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d21b4ce3-d80e-5894-92ce-668e64d91649" :knowledge-point/title "Clearing a Rational Expression With a Variable on One Side"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8c42ec6-c44c-5681-baf3-b34d487a5c25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487124}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8c42ec6-c44c-5681-baf3-b34d487a5c25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487124} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc5230bd-3f16-51ef-835b-4c76d199cbd9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487261}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "20bfc5d7-9144-5859-b1f0-27af1f1cfa84" :question/math-academy-id "q-175605" :question/problem "If $\\frac{10-3x}{4}=1$, then $x=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we clear the rational expression by multiplying the equation through by $4$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{10-3x}{4} & =1 \\\\ 4(\\frac{10-3x}{4}) & =4\\cdot 1 \\\\ \\cancel{4}(\\frac{10-3x}{\\cancel{4}}) & =4 \\\\ 10-3x & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve the remaining equation using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10-3x & =4 \\\\ 10-3x-10 & =4-10 \\\\ -3x & =-6 \\\\ \\frac{-3x}{-3} & =\\frac{-6}{-3} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-3}x}{\\cancel{-3}} & =\\frac{6}{3} \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487309 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078579 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9d60309-32e0-535d-b5fa-ef55787336c8" :knowledge-point/title "Clearing a Rational Expression With Binomials on Both Sides"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35af7295-abe0-53a4-901b-385d93918397" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486709}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35af7295-abe0-53a4-901b-385d93918397" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486709} :answer-field/id #uuid "9bb77437-7bcb-5f22-a30d-4200f3ac2fa2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487225}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2de1d7cb-6ad2-5a64-8b22-82ed6e525706" :question/math-academy-id "q-178530" :question/problem "If $5y-7=\\frac{16-5y}{2},$ then $y=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we clear the rational expression by multiplying both sides by $2.$ \nWe must make sure that all of the terms on the left-hand side are multiplied by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5y-7 & =\\frac{16-5y}{2} \\\\ 2(5y-7) & =2(\\frac{16-5y}{2}) \\\\ 2\\cdot 5y+2\\cdot (-7) & =\\cancel{2}(\\frac{16-5y}{\\cancel{2}}) \\\\ 10y-14 & =16-5y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve the remaining equation using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10y-14 & =16-5y \\\\ 10y-14+5y & =16-5y+5y \\\\ 15y-14 & =16 \\\\ 15y-14+14 & =16+14 \\\\ 15y & =30 \\\\ \\frac{15y}{15} & =\\frac{30}{15} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{15}y}{\\cancel{15}} & =\\frac{30}{15} \\\\ y & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487348 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078578 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d31a29c9-e053-557b-8f5a-3dd49b340144" :knowledge-point/title "Clearing a Rational Expression With a Variable on Both Sides"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11a5337e-2e38-5339-a515-cdcc91c5a4ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{12}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486631} {:answer/id #uuid "9db708cf-c16f-5448-be3f-8b07d17e63e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486949} {:answer/id #uuid "bde50a7e-ece4-5c06-8140-e186ffa30b0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487011} {:answer/id #uuid