\frac{7}{14} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{14}x}{\\cancel{14}} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487358 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078577 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d21b4ce3-d80e-5894-92ce-668e64d91649" :knowledge-point/title "Clearing a Rational Expression With a Variable on One Side"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11cda6f2-fa4c-533f-a5fb-5ae6d008a750" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486632} {:answer/id #uuid "2059fb78-a1d2-516b-b757-c8200d097afd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486658} {:answer/id #uuid "37d15691-b3ad-5364-a583-ab8f35061ef7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486713} {:answer/id #uuid "57ab5f7d-1a96-50a7-80d5-df0915422b13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "39" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486785} {:answer/id #uuid "b4e20d5c-83e8-599c-b953-71a78f2d26e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486993}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37d15691-b3ad-5364-a583-ab8f35061ef7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486713} :answer-field/id #uuid "69080ef7-9645-5832-a070-cafaabea87b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487193}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a03551ce-a9e0-5803-b72e-ac5c9487b91c" :question/math-academy-id "q-516" :question/problem "If $\\frac{3x-4}{5}=4$, then $x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we clear the rational expression by multiplying the equation through by $5$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3x-4}{5} & =4 \\\\ 5(\\frac{3x-4}{5}) & =5\\cdot 4 \\\\ \\cancel{5}(\\frac{3x-4}{\\cancel{5}}) & =20 \\\\ 3x-4 & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve the remaining equation using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-4 & =20 \\\\ 3x-4+4 & =20+4 \\\\ 3x & =24 \\\\ \\frac{3x}{3} & =\\frac{24}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{3}x}{\\cancel{3}} & =\\frac{24}{3} \\\\ x & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
